Summary:
Today’s session involved practicing a Data Structures and Algorithms problem based on an “Easy Food” concept. The task focused on designing a system where different food items were assigned taste values, and users were allowed to taste any food multiple times. Logic was developed to reduce the taste value of a food item after repeated selections while still allowing flexible combinations of choices. The implementation also included displaying the selected food items along with their updated values and calculating the final total taste score.

Outcomes:
The problem-solving session improved understanding of algorithm design, conditional logic, and handling repeated operations within a dataset. A working solution was developed to manage food selections, update taste values dynamically, and generate the final total taste value accurately. The practice strengthened skills related to arrays, loops, and data handling in DSA. This activity also helped in improving analytical thinking and logical implementation of real-world inspired problem statements.
